WEBVTT

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:02.380
Mornin'.

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.730
Hey, morning.

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:04.070
It was somethin' else.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.270
Ah, I wish I coulda seen it.
It was somethin' else.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:05.940
Ah, I wish I coulda seen it.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.370
Good morning!

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.760
Good morning to you too.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.870
<i>My name is Nagito Komaeda.</i>

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.250
<i>I'm just a run-of-the-mill guy who goes to a run-of-the-mill school.</i>

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:19.330
<i>There's only one thing really exceptional about me...</i>

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.270
I'm gonna be late!

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.670
Yeesh, I have the worst luck.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.310
Just an ordinary teenage boy?

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:52.280
Nagito Komaeda and the World Destroyer

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.750
Owwww...

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.060
You should really watch where you're walking,

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.490
buttercup

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:01.190
I—

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:02.980
I'm sorry.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:04.620
Don't mention it, darling.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.620
<i>There are people in this world</i>

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.660
<i>with talent great enough to shape the foundation of society.</i>

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.830
<i>I'm not one of them.</i>

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.240
<i>I'm just another face in the crowd.</i>

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:17.810
<i>Which isn't to say I envy them, though.</i>

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.820
<i>No, it's much easier being a nobody.</i>

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:25.980
<i>The star of the show is such a restrictive, demanding role.</i>

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.700
'Sup?

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.830
You look like you got run through a woodchipper, bud.

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.550
What the hell happened?

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:33.820
Some chestnuts fell on me, that's all.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.400
You should stop by the nurse's office.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:38.620
I will, thanks.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.510
Good morning, everyone.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.750
Took ya long enough—

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.720
Wha— Aaah!

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:54.710
Is it just me,

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.680
or are you even <i>more</i>
beat up than before?

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.960
I'm sho showwy!

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.390
It'h all my faulth!

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.880
Don't blame yourself, Tsumiki.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.730
If anyone's at fault here, it's me.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.060
While she was patching me up in the nurse's office,

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:14.480
someone outside hit a home run... right through the window.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:19.840
And that was that.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.910
He did autograph the ball for me as an apology, though.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:23.730
I'm so sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.830
You got it pretty rough, don'tcha?
I'm so sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.870
Oh no, I wouldn't say that.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:33.340
I believe that there's a fixed quantity of "luck" in the world,

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:40.050
which means that the more bad luck I have,
the more good luck that leaves for others.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.900
Can you think of a greater honor

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:46.840
than a nobody like me knowing they can still make the world a better place for everyone?

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.850
Yeah, I can think of a thousand.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.980
Aah! Good morning, Sonia!

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.420
Fancy meeting you here!

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:56.180
Oh, how fortunate I am!

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:58.190
This is our classroom.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:01.910
There is nothing fanciful about our encounter, you silly man.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:07.000
It's a wonderful thing to see someone find happiness when their dreams come true.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.180
You got any dreams?

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.420
Me?

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:15.130
No, I'm a nobody.
I'm too insignificant to have a dream.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.590
Nice dodge.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:21.810
You know, if you dropped the whole "nobody" act
and showed your true colors,

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.430
I bet you'd make one helluva splash.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.140
Oh, no.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.450
It's not an act,

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:32.150
and I don't have enough talent to make even a tiny little ripple.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.340
Have you ever actually <i>tried</i>?

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.280
I'll leave the trying to those who have real talent.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.950
'Sup, losers?

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.750
How's it hangin'?

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.410
You're calling <i>us</i> losers?

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.360
Did something happen?

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.370
You're giving me the damned creeps, man.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:53.620
So I asked Sonia,

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.380
"Care to join me for refreshments after class?"

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.380
And guess what she said?

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.260
"Why, certainly."

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.340
She said yes!

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.050
Oh. Good for you.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:05.010
That's wonderful!

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:09.490
Your lifelong dream has finally come true, Souda!

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:12.700
I'm so, so very happy for you!

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:15.440
Y-Yeah... thanks.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.910
But I mean, we're just meetin' up at a café, that's all.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.200
Good morning!

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.440
Everyone back to your seats.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.660
It's time for homeroom.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.260
All rise!

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.380
Bow!

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:39.840
Be seated!

00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:58.650
The hell you so relieved about?

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.610
You're not plannin' to ditch, are you? You pussy.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.030
Pussy?

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.590
Guess I am.

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:05.710
C'mon, man.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.120
What's the matter?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.330
You seemed so excited this morning.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.080
Can you blame me?

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:14.980
You've seen how pretty Sonia is.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.020
She may say some kinda bizarre stuff sometimes,

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:21.100
but she's smart, and she's literally a princess on top of that.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.400
So what you're sayin' is she's too good for you?

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.760
Damn straight, she is!

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.360
I'm just...

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.550
I'm just a kid who likes to play with machines.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.410
Anyone could tell you I'm not worth a second of her time.

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:33.720
So I can't...

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.210
Why the hell're you worried about being suitable?
So I can't...

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:36.730
Why the hell're you worried about being suitable?

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:39.610
You're not even dating!

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.190
Social status be damned, a man doesn't back down on his word. Period.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:43.980
You're right!

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:45.260
You're absolutely right!

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:47.320
But I'm not the kind of man you are!

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:50.810
Souda, it's talent that you desire, isn't it?

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:51.620
Huh?

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:55.480
Compared to a princess like Sonia, you're inconsequential.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.100
And that makes you anxious.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.360
I understand that feeling.

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:02.830
Talent? Maybe you're right...

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:04.900
For god's sake.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:08.300
Grow a pair! Talent doesn't matter a damned bit!

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:12.940
Your machismo could be considered a sort of talent as well, Kuzuryuu.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:15.640
That's being counterproductive here, man...

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:16.930
All right, fine.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.600
So what about us without talent? What do we do?

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.320
Find happiness.

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:23.270
What?

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:24.980
Look around.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:28.990
The vast majority of society consists of talentless nobodies,

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:32.450
but they've still managed to find some degree of happiness.

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:35.430
See? You don't <i>need</i> talent.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.170
Talent is merely a shackle,

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:43.140
and the greater it is, the more it obstructs your search for happiness.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:49.050
Sonia being a princess
doesn't mean she has a perfect life.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:51.510
That's... a good point.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:52.620
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:56.260
Now go on. Don't keep Sonia waiting.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.020
Yeah.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.230
Thanks, bud!

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:08.040
I'm impressed. Guess not everything
that comes outta your mouth is noise.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.510
Now that's harsh.

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:15.120
Have you heard yourself when you start rambling?
You're so far off-the-wall it's scary.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:18.160
But you landed this one perfectly.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:20.110
Thank you,

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.580
I suppose?

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:31.630
Ahh, if only the world were free of talent.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:32.460
Huh?

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:33.470
Think about it.

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:36.890
If Sonia weren't a princess but an ordinary girl,

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:40.360
Souda wouldn't have had anything to worry about in the first place.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.650
Uh, I guess?

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:43.870
I...

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:46.370
I despise talent.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:52.320
Were I able, I would erase all talent from the world entirely.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:55.530
Without talent,

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:57.790
everyone would be able to lead modest lives,

00:07:58.090 --> 00:08:00.750
find a modest amount of happiness.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:04.710
Don't you think that would be wonderful?

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.400
Back off.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:11.000
Huh?

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.840
I said back off already.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:15.410
I take it back—you're still a creep.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:17.560
Oh, uh, I'm sorry.

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:20.650
I mean, it's fine. It's who you are.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:23.400
Anyway, whaddya say we grab a drink,

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:25.010
get a head start on celebratin' for Souda?

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:27.520
Uh... we're still in high school, though.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.980
They're non-alcoholic—

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.430
if anyone asks.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:42.200
I'm so sorryyyy...

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.710
Did you not get the memo, Nagito?

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:50.050
<i>I'm</i> the only one who's allowed to beat up on Mikan.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:55.430
Jeez, I really do have the worst luck.

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:59.390
I'm tempted to call <i>that</i> its own kind of talent.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:10.380
It would seem this is as deep as I can go.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:12.680
So this world, then,

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:15.990
is the lowest stratum?

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:20.850
There is no saving this.
I have no choice but to destroy it.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:26.140
How dull.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.350
How dreadfully dull.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:26.800
That's what I've been told.

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:28.620
And we're sure that's the case?

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:31.510
Goddammit.

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:34.300
Is something the matter?

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.250
I just got word...

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:38.420
Souda was murdered.

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:40.220
No way...

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:41.280
I thought it was an accident?

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:42.600
Nope.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.000
They messed him up real bad too.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.630
I've gotta go.

00:10:46.630 --> 00:10:48.220
You take care o' things here.

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:51.050
Go where?

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:52.590
The funeral's about to begin.

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.150
Where the hell do you think?

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:56.210
To catch the bastard who did this.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.220
You can't—

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.550
it's too dangerous.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:01.060
Let the police handle it.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.890
He was a brother to me.

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:07.020
Just be careful.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.360
So you comin' or not?

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:11.250
I wouldn't be any help.

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:13.310
I'd only get in your way.

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:16.040
Well, that's your choice.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:17.170
Wait a second!

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:19.920
I shall accompany you.

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:22.870
Now, now, little lady,

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:25.830
you don't have any place where I'm goin'.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.580
Stay your tongue.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:30.620
No one tells Sonia Nevermind what she can and cannot do.

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:32.540
And that includes you.

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:37.000
You wanna tag along? Be my damn guest.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.000
That I shall.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.310
How...

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.980
How could this happen?

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:10.370
<i>There are people in this world</i>

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:14.790
<i>with talent great enough to shape the foundation of society.</i>

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:18.500
<i>I'm not one of them.</i>

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:20.710
<i>I'm just another face in the crowd.</i>

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:23.740
<i>Which isn't to say I envy them, though.</i>

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:27.140
<i>No, it's much easier being a nobody.</i>

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:30.700
<i>The star of the show is such a restrictive, demanding role.</i>

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.860
<i>Were there no talent,</i>

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.320
<i>everyone would be able to lead modest lives...</i>

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:43.240
<i>find a modest amount of happiness...</i>

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:54.620
Hey, dickwad!

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.410
Right on schedule.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.550
You got some balls layin' a hand on my brother!

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:05.830
Sire!

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:12.100
So who the hell are you?!

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:13.840
The World...

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.060
Destroyer.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.710
World Destroyer?

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:19.430
Lose your head up there in the clouds?

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:22.950
Was it truly you who killed Souda?

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:26.490
From your perspective,
that would indeed be the case.

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:29.440
Why would you do such a thing?

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:33.450
In order to destroy... this world.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:34.930
Why did Souda have to—

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.560
The "who" was irrelevant.

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:40.630
Any of his friends would have sufficed.

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:44.520
You're just a damned terrorist with a dozen loose screws.

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:48.720
H-Hey!

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:49.550
Strike first,

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:51.110
and strike hard!

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:01.460
Hello?

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:04.190
<i>Komaeda...</i>

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:05.470
<i>Good, you're safe...</i>

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:07.000
Pekoyama?

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:10.870
<i>Please... listen carefully...
There's not much time...</i>

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:14.210
The man who murdered Souda...

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:15.510
is after you...

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:17.070
<i>Wh-What?</i>

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:20.490
He has short hair... and red eyes...

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:21.820
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.700
Listen.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:27.140
You made the correct call.

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:29.320
You wouldn't stand a chance against him.

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:31.530
You were right to run.

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:32.050
<i>Tell me!</i>

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:34.530
Where are you?! What happened?!

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:36.560
<i>Fuyuhiko said to tell you...</i>

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.040
<i>not to blame yourself...</i>

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.790
Not to blame myself?

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:42.020
For what?!

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:44.660
<i>Keep yourself alive... so that one day...</i>

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.470
<i>you can avenge Fuyuhiko for me...</i>

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.070
Avenge him?!

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:50.860
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:52.230
<i>That I...</i>

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:55.330
<i>I failed to protect him...</i>

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:26.540
<i>Am I speaking to Nagito Komaeda?</i>

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:28.360
Who are you?

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:29.890
The World...

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:31.820
Destroyer.

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:37.210
<i>Has your world crumbled yet?</i>

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:38.150
Huh?

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:40.520
<i>It would seem not.</i>

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:42.020
What are you talking about?

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:44.840
<i>Then I shall proceed until it has.</i>

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.010
<i>One by one.</i>

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:49.070
<i>Piece by piece.</i>

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:50.170
<i>I will tear it down.</i>

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.550
<i>I will leave nothing behind.</i>

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:55.100
<i>I will offer no mercy.</i>

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:57.610
<i>I will spare no one.</i>

00:15:58.310 --> 00:15:59.270
I've heard enough!

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:37.660
I did not anticipate you would show up so soon.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:41.590
I expected I would have to delete another ten of your friends.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.040
Neither Kuzuryuu,

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:47.520
nor Pekoyama, nor Sonia

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.480
were by any means pushovers.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:52.550
You must possess a great deal of talent

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:55.950
to be able to take them out so easily.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:57.780
You see, I...

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:00.420
I despise talent.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:05.700
Were I able, I would erase all talent from the world entirely.

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:07.600
And I've never felt that so strongly.

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:09.420
So you...

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:11.690
have to go.

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:17.440
And how do you plan to get rid of me
with no talent of your own?

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:22.810
I won't deny I'm just a regular guy with a bit of an unlucky streak.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.460
I don't belong anywhere near the spotlight.

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:30.150
See?

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:33.430
Anything I do turns out badly for me.

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:35.570
I could never come out of this on top.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:37.160
But you know what?

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:40.890
Even though I lack any real talent,

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:43.260
I can't see myself losing to you either.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:51.880
What you're feeling is called "hope."

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:53.470
"Hope"?

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:54.890
Hope...?

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:56.340
What a peculiar-sounding word.

00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:58.540
Although,

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:00.350
I feel like I've heard it before.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:02.750
All right, then,

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:05.640
let's see what that "hope" can achieve!

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:17.320
I have such terrible luck.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:20.660
I couldn't possibly defeat you.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.410
But maybe I can take you out with me.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.720
Imagine how incredibly unlucky you'd have to be

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:30.000
to make a whole building collapse by merely throwing a ball—

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.630
even if it <i>was</i> already falling apart.

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:36.350
<i>Kuzuryuu...</i>

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:39.050
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:19.050
World destruction complete.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:27.450
At last, free from that illusion.

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:32.440
We're inside the Neo World Program, aren't we?

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.000
Indeed.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:36.920
That was definitely a world in need of destroying.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:39.560
And you're Izuru Kamukura, I take it?

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:45.080
More precisely, I am an Alter Ego
modified to perform psychodives.

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:49.480
After your death within the Neo World Program,

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:52.020
the data containing your psyche was successfully restored;

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:56.430
however, the traumatic circumstances
of your death caused psychological instability.

00:19:56.430 --> 00:19:59.550
My task was to eliminate that instability.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:01.500
So what you're saying is...

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:05.260
everyone in there was all in my head?

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.120
Yes.

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:09.050
Your fourteen classmates

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:12.300
were each a fragment of your psyche

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:15.690
which also served as psychological defense mechanisms.

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:18.300
Hence ten more friends to delete.

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:20.100
Tell me,

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:22.580
was all of that being monitored from the outside?

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:25.700
No. Your personal privacy
is of the utmost importance.

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:27.510
Thank goodness.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:33.080
I can't believe I actually said
I wanted a world without any talent

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.640
if it meant everyone could find happiness.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:38.420
That's just not who I am.

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:41.390
That world, and the people inhabiting it,

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:43.410
were a reflection of your own desires.

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:45.890
One of many possible outcomes.

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:50.320
What might have been if one Nagito Komaeda

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:53.860
lacked his good fortune
and led a quiet, uneventful life.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:59.270
I'll pass on that "possibility."

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:02.770
What the world needs is hope—

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:07.100
immense hope born from equally immense talent.

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:14.210
Alter Ego, all assigned tasks executed successfully.

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:27.140
Hey! Can you hear me?

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:34.600
Ahh... Izuru Kamukura?

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:36.330
No,

00:21:36.970 --> 00:21:38.730
you're, uh, Hajime Hinata, right?

00:21:41.470 --> 00:21:42.980
They're both me.

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:47.400
I suppose I should thank you for waking me up?

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:50.590
I knew you'd make it to the lowest stratum—

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:52.570
I believed in you.

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:53.700
How are the others?

00:21:55.170 --> 00:21:57.430
You're the last one out.

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:13.610
You were in there long enough.

00:22:13.610 --> 00:22:15.520
What kinda dream were you havin'?

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:17.450
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:22:17.450 --> 00:22:18.980
I overslept a bit.

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:21.820
Dreaming about a buncha pretty girls, were ya?

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:24.230
Whoa!

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:25.690
The hell're you doing?!

00:22:25.690 --> 00:22:29.160
It wasn't a bad dream, at least.

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:31.740
Hey! Get off me!

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:32.910
You damn creep!

00:22:32.930 --> 00:22:34.620
Let's get going, then, shall we?

00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:36.160
Yes,

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:38.540
let's set off,

00:22:38.990 --> 00:22:40.500
in the name of hope.
